1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,057
How do Twitch Auto Clips work?

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:10,907
Auto Clips are Twitch's own automatic clips, and they're still in limited testing, so not every channel has them.

3
00:00:10,907 --> 00:00:14,137
If yours doesn't, paste the Twitch VOD into ClipMe.

4
00:00:14,137 --> 00:00:17,937
It ranks the whole stream and cuts captioned vertical clips.

5
00:00:18,887 --> 00:00:22,036
Auto Clips depend on Twitch letting your channel in.

6
00:00:22,036 --> 00:00:24,519
ClipMe works on any Twitch VOD you paste.

7
00:00:25,469 --> 00:00:31,058
It reads Twitch chat, and chat activity is one of the signals ClipMe uses to rank each moment.

8
00:00:32,008 --> 00:00:33,608
And it isn't Twitch-only.

9
00:00:33,608 --> 00:00:36,232
Paste a Kick or YouTube VOD the same way.

10
00:00:37,182 --> 00:00:40,801
See the best auto clippers for streamers at clipme.com.

11
00:00:40,801 --> 00:00:42,643
Paste a VOD and try it free.

